WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.440
- Our next guest is a
12-time Grammy-nominated,

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.565
multi-Platinum rap star.

00:00:04.565 --> 00:00:06.580
My band is really excited.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.960
They were just playing.
They were freaking out.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.170
They're very excited.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.417
His latest album is called

00:00:10.417 --> 00:00:14.130
"Extinction Level Event
2: The Wrath of God,"

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.220
AKA 2020, and it's out now.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.320
Please give it up for Busta Rhymes, y'all.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.510
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:25.330
Yeah! Lester played
those, he's very excited.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:26.690
Alright, well, we've been talking.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:28.389
What's up, Busta?

00:00:28.389 --> 00:00:30.120
- What's up, Kelly, how you doing?

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.670
- I'm living my best life, talking to you.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.253
I'm having a good day.

00:00:36.341 --> 00:00:38.060
- My type of talk. I love to hear that.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.890
- Oh my God, I love the
title of your album.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.660
I've actually renamed it AKA 2020

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.209
'cause it feels like it could be that.

00:00:45.209 --> 00:00:48.570
We've actually been talking
about motivational words

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.350
for the new year, just to
kind of keep everybody's

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.250
kind of positivity going and
maybe have a fresh start.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.643
Is there a creative kind of
mantra or a certain mantra

00:00:57.643 --> 00:00:59.190
that you live by?

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:04.190
- My favorite tool is,
failure is never an option.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.940
And the next one is to
be, you gotta be swift

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:11.422
and changeable in order to be remaindable.

00:01:11.422 --> 00:01:12.654
- Whoa, what? Remaindable?

00:01:12.654 --> 00:01:14.030
I ain't even heard. That's nice.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.720
But I also notice though,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.680
you were really motivated
to get fit this year.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.060
I wish that had happened to me,

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:21.293
but can we see the photos

00:01:21.293 --> 00:01:23.830
to represent what I'm talking about?

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:28.830
What the hell? What are you
doing, asking for a friend?

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.030
- I think the beautiful thing in life

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:37.030
is the hill and the gully ride, you know.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.193
- Yeah.

00:01:38.193 --> 00:01:40.950
- And I was really going through probably

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.810
one of my most challenging
times in my life.

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:50.600
I've had some lows, like we all go in.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.350
None of us exempt from
actually going through

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.010
some sort of hardship,

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:58.613
but I lost my dad in, I believe, 2014,

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.760
and I didn't deal with it
in, like, a real, like,

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:04.593
mourning way.

00:02:04.593 --> 00:02:06.522
I kind of just drowned myself in work.

00:02:06.522 --> 00:02:07.560
- Yeah.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.520
- And I kind of really
neglected to take care of me.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.123
I was at about 340 pounds.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.343
I was having issues with my health,

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.530
and wasn't telling anybody.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.630
I had blood, I was on
blood pressure medicine.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:26.890
I was on two blood pressure
medicines, by the way.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.680
I was on a acid reflux medicine.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.510
And I also had a horrible sleep apnea,

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:38.330
and I was also growing
pallets on my throat.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:42.590
And it just reached an apex
and it got to a point where,

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:45.450
you know, my son, my oldest son,

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.600
who I had working as my
road manager at the time

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:53.430
was so disappointed at what he saw in me.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:56.210
And I never heard that from my son before.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.160
So, it was a crossroads,

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.430
and I wasn't happy with
the way I was feeling

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.622
and the way I was looking at myself.

00:03:02.622 --> 00:03:05.920
And I knew in order to put this music out,

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.540
I needed to not just sound incredible,

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.030
but I needed to feel incredible,

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.580
and I needed to look incredible.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.019
And I wanted to make sure that I had

00:03:13.019 --> 00:03:17.380
successfully executed doing everything

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.390
that I was able to do within my means

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.730
and within my control
and within my ability

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:26.370
to not leave a stone unturned

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:29.550
when it came to securing this win,

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:33.340
which is probably one of
my greatest wins ever.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.670
- Oh, that feels, that's
gotta feel great, man.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.330
Like, I do know that feeling

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:38.660
when you work on something
and you're like, man,

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:41.390
I don't even care how
it works out out there.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:43.360
It got out of me. I'm so proud of it.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.880
I did it. That's got to feel amazing.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:49.760
And I heard, I just want
to know if this is true.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.914
My brother actually
turned me on to your music

00:03:51.914 --> 00:03:54.799
when I was really young,
probably too young,

00:03:54.799 --> 00:03:57.730
but I loved it.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.300
And I have to say though,

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.820
I heard that your, you,
actually, your first time,

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:05.940
your first, like, rap
name wasn't Busta Rhymes.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:06.773
Did you? You had another?

00:04:06.773 --> 00:04:08.390
- No, it wasn't.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:13.160
Yeah. My first solo
album came out in 1996,

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.650
but my first record that I ever put out

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:20.580
came out in 1991 with my group,
Leaders of the New School.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.560
And Chuck D from Public Enemy

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.330
actually gave us the group name

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.773
Leaders of the New School,

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:32.963
but my first rap name was Chill-O-Ski,

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.963
and there was nothing cool about that.

00:04:39.096 --> 00:04:39.929
- Like -

00:04:39.929 --> 00:04:41.880
- Don't laugh at me,
Kelly, don't laugh at me.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.390
- Well, I just, I love it because

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:46.170
I just have always known
you like since forever,

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:47.860
so I cannot picture you with another name

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:48.860
other than Busta Rhymes.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.630
That's so fitting, like,
you're Busta Rhymes.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:52.233
Like, you are not Chill-O-Ski.

00:04:53.638 --> 00:04:55.930
- I'm definitely not.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:59.550
And you know, when
Chuck D said that to me,

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.160
that my name should be Busta Rhymes,

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.140
I was like, I don't like that name.

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:05.750
Why should I be, why would you pick that

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:06.690
out of all names for me?

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:07.523
- [Kelly] You gonna bust a rhyme someone.

00:05:07.523 --> 00:05:10.540
- Right, but that's, he said, you know,

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.173
Leaders of the New School is a statement.

00:05:13.173 --> 00:05:16.160
You know, if you're going
to be leading the new school

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.610
in the new era of hip
hop and MCs and rappers

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:23.270
and you're going to be a significant part

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:26.050
of the climate shift in the culture,

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:29.993
then you gotta represent
that from your name first.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.320
They used to always
ask me to bust a rhyme,

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:35.430
so it was kind of synonymous with that.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.403
But whenever I did, you know,

00:05:38.403 --> 00:05:42.100
get my opportunity to bust a
rhyme or to rap for anybody

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.950
when they asked me to,

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:48.101
I just had such a
charismatic and animated way,

00:05:48.101 --> 00:05:51.500
you know what y'all know and love me for.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:54.810
And I've been consistent
with that since day one.

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:58.430
So, Chuck D said that
it kind of reminded him,

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:00.561
my aggression in my performance,

00:06:00.561 --> 00:06:02.449
my animation in my performance,

00:06:02.449 --> 00:06:05.710
it reminded him of the legendary

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:09.240
Minnesota Vikings
football player from 1985,

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:12.430
whose actual real name,
first and last name

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:14.220
is Buster Rhymes.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.270
So -

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:17.207
- Oh my gosh. I did not know that.

00:06:17.207 --> 00:06:18.670
- So, I trusted his judgment.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:21.640
I tried it, and it ended up sticking.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:24.389
And once the world got ahold
of it and fell in love with it,

00:06:24.389 --> 00:06:26.790
I ended up eventually
falling in love with it.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:28.259
- Yeah, well, and it sounds like,

00:06:28.259 --> 00:06:31.510
I love that it wasn't
just about your music.

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:34.540
It was like your sway on all of culture,

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.100
like you were going to
be a part of a movement.

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:37.590
I love that he thought big like that,

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:39.740
so quite the visionary as well.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:41.717
Everybody, Busta's new album,

00:06:41.717 --> 00:06:44.970
"Extinction Level Event 2:
The Wrath of God" is out now.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.153
You gotta check it out.

